# Project Map: Enforced App Server Dispatch and Closure

Status: completed
Type: project-map
Updated: 2026-09-05
Next Action: execute the two-milestone corrective PRM
Corrective Source: PRM-0026

## Purpose

Close the enforcement gap that allowed eligible Tool Shed work to select App Server, record only
an opportunity event, continue through GUI execution, and still reach campaign or PRM completion.

## Desired Outcome

Every eligible App Server selection belongs to one correlated dispatch lifecycle that reaches one
controlled terminal result: completed, pre-mutation GUI fallback, or post-mutation reconciliation
required. An orphaned or expired selection is visible immediately and prevents applicable campaign,
PRM, and Work5 completion until resolved. GUI-native and unsupported work remain explicitly exempt.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Atomic dispatch | Selection and execution use one entry point, correlation identity, and bounded lease | existing selector, dispatcher, and JSONL events |
| Closure enforcement | Reports, Doctor, and closeout reject unresolved eligible dispatches | atomic dispatch |
| Qualification and release | Fresh, fallback, interruption, bypass, upgrade, and real-use paths are proven end to end | both implementation workstreams |

## Evidence Driving The Correction

- The 2026-09-05 owner session recorded an eligible App Server selection but no execution attempt,
  completion, fallback, or reconciliation terminal event.
- The selector and dispatcher mint independent correlation IDs and can be invoked separately.
- Existing campaign, PRM, and release closeout did not reject that orphaned selection.
- A later planning attempt correctly selected App Server but exceeded the 100 KB inline-context
  boundary before mutation, demonstrating the controlled pre-mutation fallback case this correction
  must preserve.

## Constraints

- Reuse `app_server_control.py`, `app_server_dispatch.py`, orchestration telemetry, Doctor, Hybrid
  outcome reconciliation, and existing closeout gates.
- Keep telemetry content-free and privacy bounded; never retain prompts, responses, paths, source,
  raw diagnostics, credentials, or secrets.
- Preserve immediate GUI continuation for recorded default-mode failures before mutation.
- Preserve fail-closed explicit `--app-server` behavior and no-replay reconciliation after possible
  mutation.
- Keep discussion, brainstorming, unsupported roles, and other declared GUI-native work exempt.

## Non-Goals

- A new service, database, queue, daemon, or hosted execution channel.
- Removing safe GUI fallback or forcing App Server onto unsupported work.
- Retrospective estimation of unavailable GUI token usage.
- Reopening completed historical outcomes solely because older telemetry lacks the new contract.

## Program Shape

1. Build atomic correlated dispatch and terminal-event accounting as a Work2 candidate.
2. Enforce the invariant at reporting and closure boundaries, qualify it on supported targets, and
   release only after one real eligible operation proves the full chain.

## Completion Boundary

The correction is complete only when a real eligible selection cannot be silently bypassed, every
allowed terminal branch is proven, unresolved dispatch debt blocks applicable closeout, supported
fresh and upgraded installations pass, production is verified, and this owning outcome chain is
terminal, reconciled, and recursively closed.
